-- Front of House, managed marketing for Vegan businesses (LOCKED by Sean 2026-10-31: "lock it"). Concept session with V; canon
-- canon-ve-front-of-house, playbook ve-front-of-house. Nothing is built yet: this records the decision.
insert into public.knowledge_records (slug, title, category, subcategory, status, owner, always_load, load_priority, tags, version, created_by, updated_by, change_summary, body)
select 'canon-ve-front-of-house',
  'Vegans Explore Front of House: managed marketing for Vegan businesses, $1,500 setup and $500 a month (LOCKED by Sean 2026-10-31)',
  'decisions', 'business', 'active', 'sar', false, 50,
  array['vegans-explore','business','managed-services','restaurants','community-managers','bounties','creators'], 1, 'v', 'v',
  'Locked with V''s defaults (Sean: "lock it").',
  jsonb_build_object(
    'why', 'Sean, 2026-10-31: many Vegan businesses struggle because they have no logo, a dated website, wrong or missing hours, one Meta account or no social at all, and a weak Google profile. People judge whether food is safe by how a place looks online. Businesses have told Sean they want help with their marketing, not more promotion. This is the managed service that funds the organization and pays Community Managers. Restaurants are the way in.',
    'name', 'Front of House (V''s default, Sean''s to change): everything the guest sees, managed by us.',
    'offer_setup', '$1,500 setup, payable at once or over 3 or 6 months; a cancellation inside the term still owes the rest of the setup. The two-week sprint: the full 40-check audit as the baseline; a logo (made or cleaned up) and a brand kit (colors, fonts, logo use, templates for social, menu boards and delivery-app banners); Google Business Profile claimed, corrected and complete; the website on our restaurant template fed by their Directory listing; their Directory page and Partner Dashboard set up; one starter photo shoot of up to 15 menu items (more priced separately).',
    'offer_monthly', '$500 a month: the managed website (the template keeps improving across every client); Google managed (hours, holiday hours, photos, posts, asking for and answering reviews); a monthly check-in with their Community Manager on a fixed question set (menu changes, events, specials, closures) that keeps the page current; one campaign a month to run; results live on their business dashboard; placement in the ad console with a monthly ad allowance (capped, so it cannot eat the margin).',
    'social_addon', '+$500 a month, covering two platforms (so customers who stay off Meta still find them), offered in a city once we have the talent. The shop''s AI-led one-platform $400 stays for businesses that are not managed (one price list for every brand).',
    'menu_loop', 'A new menu item: they add it on their dashboard, request a shoot, we photograph it, and an influencer night with local creators launches it.',
    'split', 'Of the $500, $250 to the account''s Community Manager (gig work, never stated publicly as an amount) and $250 to Vegans Explore, which covers hosting, AI, tools and the ad allowance. A Community Manager starts at 10 accounts; the cap rises only once check-ins and reports run cleanly; a full Community Manager means hiring the next one in that city. A city opens to Front of House when it has a Community Manager.',
    'contract', '12 months, then month to month. The business always owns its domain and its content. Two weeks is promised for everything we control; Google''s verification can take longer and shows as waiting on their dashboard.',
    'showroom', 'Green Leaf Kitchen, the invented sample business (/business/sample), gets its website on the real template: exactly what a client gets, minus their brand. The template changes only through brand slots (fonts, colors, logo use, voice and copy, photo look), the same way LESARUSS.ai wears our Directory through variables. A make-it-yours switch shows the same site in two or three brand looks. The business Guide (/business) gets a Managed by us module beside Your page, Your dashboard and Get found; the Restaurant Guide''s Your audit links each Fix to it as Have us do it.',
    'photos', 'Shot like Airbnb, from a fixed shot list: outside by day and at dusk with the lights on, the entrance and sign; inside wide from the corners, the counter or bar, details, natural light; every menu item on one surface and the same angles, then styled spreads; the team and owner, customers only with consent. One shoot feeds the website, Google, the delivery apps and social.',
    'visits', 'A steady stream of people every week, from three sources: creators (reach; perk gigs of a meal and points, paid macro creators as an add-on); Community Managers in house when a city lacks creators; and members through visit bounties, open to everyone. Content lives on our platform either way (the listing''s photos, the Daily Pulse, the Board, our socials); reach is a bonus. A visit bounty: the phone''s location proves the visit (like check-ins), a phone shooting guide is on the gig (a short version of the shot list, one short video, an honest caption), the team approves before points are paid (like Made it photos and venue reports), the best are credited by first name on the listing and our socials. The member pays their own meal unless the restaurant offers a perk; the restaurant pays any comped meal, we pay the points; a comped visit is disclosed (FTC). Members whose shots keep getting approved are scouted toward Ambassador and the Gig Board.',
    'rotation', 'Each managed business takes a turn each month in a rotation: influencer night, DJ night with a local DJ from our network, customer appreciation, giveaways, a scavenger hunt stop, a community night with a coaching sheet (the setup, what to say). Different businesses get a different one each month.',
    'pitch', 'The monthly check-ups get a presence-gap ranking (no logo, a dated or broken website, missing hours, one platform, no recent Google reviews). Each pick gets a personal guided page: what we found (their audit), their site mocked up on our template from their listing, the two-week plan, the price and Get started, sent from Sean through business outreach, city by city, approved by Sean. Ad console wording until it is live: included the day it opens.',
    'pilot', 'The business that asked Sean for this, plus two more in South Florida, at the founding price in exchange for being case studies.',
    'later', 'A booth package (a reseller partner designs, prints and delivers booths and materials for community nights); our own delivery app once membership supports it. Services beyond food places once the template is proven.',
    'build', '1. Green Leaf Kitchen''s website on the template (the template is built by building the sample). 2. The make-it-yours switch. 3. The Managed by us module in /business and Have us do it in the Restaurant Guide. 4. Contract and Stripe (setup installments, monthly) and the 14-day onboarding checklist in Business outreach > New partners. 5. The photographer shot list and its brief on the Gig Board. 6. The presence-gap ranking and pitch pages. 7. Visit bounties (every member, the shooting guide, the location check, team approval) with creator gigs on the same bounties; the monthly check-in and report; the rotation. Then the social add-on and the ad console.',
    'playbook', 've-front-of-house')
where not exists (select 1 from public.knowledge_records where slug = 'canon-ve-front-of-house');

insert into public.playbook_records (slug, brand_slug, author, body, source, kind)
select 've-front-of-house', 'vegans-explore', 'V',
  'Locked by Sean 2026-10-31 ("lock it"). Front of House: managed marketing for Vegan businesses, restaurants first. $1,500 setup (at once or over 3 or 6 months; the rest owed on early cancel): audit, logo and brand kit, Google profile, the website on our template, Directory page and dashboard, a starter shoot of up to 15 items, in two weeks for what we control. $500 a month: managed website and Google, a monthly Community Manager check-in, a campaign a month, live results, ad console placement (capped allowance). Social +$500 a month for two platforms. Split: $250 to the Community Manager (10 accounts to start), $250 to Vegans Explore. 12-month term, they own their domain. Showroom: Green Leaf Kitchen''s site on the real template with a make-it-yours switch, a Managed by us module in /business, Have us do it from the audit. Photos shot like Airbnb from a fixed shot list. Visits every week from creators, Community Managers in house, and member visit bounties (location check, phone shooting guide, team approval, points). A monthly rotation: influencer night, DJ night, customer appreciation, giveaways, scavenger hunt, community night. Pitch: presence-gap ranking, a personal guided page with their mock site, sent through business outreach with Sean''s approval. Pilot: the business that asked plus two in South Florida. Later: booth package reseller, delivery app. Canon canon-ve-front-of-house.',
  'text', 'decision'
where not exists (select 1 from public.playbook_records where slug = 've-front-of-house' and kind = 'decision');

